From e0d08b206904829e3e774b5f3b3248fe7ca323b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:18:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Score sustained multi-station traffic rises in the RF monitor

Add a bounded traffic-rise part (up to 10 points) to the Propagation
Monitor score. It counts only when the deduplicated packet rate in the
window is at least 3x the coverage-weighted baseline rate, at least 5
unique stations were heard and that count is at least 1.5x the baseline
per-hour unique count, and window observations span 20 minutes. Full
credit at 6x. It is zero without a usable baseline and cannot raise an
alert on its own (the possible threshold is 40 at Medium).

The owner-reported overnight sample on SNOMAN HQ (about 2.1x baseline,
7 forwarded stations) scores 0 traffic points and stays Normal. Tests
cover that case, a sustained multi-station rise, and a single-station
burst. Thresholds are untested hypotheses and configurable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019jwdUNLdgFDTkdkrPTAK1B
